KG42.register("rules-8cf3a5c17bf72644520dceca",{"id":"11-p2p_mechanisms_evaluation::v141-c-R018","paper":"11-p2p_mechanisms_evaluation","record":{"rule_id":"v141-c-R018","mechanism_id":"v141-a-M03","name":"Supply submission","process_stage":"bidding","market_meaning":"The BS supply submission must use the energy-bid format specified by Formula (A18), the same format required by SDR. Scope: Supply quantities within the energy bids required by the BS mechanism.","independence_rationale":"Relations governed by the approved function bidding.supply under the fixed relation-ownership template. Conditional branches retain their explicit scope in local constraints.","V":["bidding.supply"],"E":[],"omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"bidding","context_text":"Supply quantities within the energy bids required by the BS mechanism.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g07-ev-08"]},"x":[],"theta":[],"phi":[{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R018-C001","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"The BS supply submission must use the energy-bid format specified by Formula (A18), the same format required by SDR. Scope: Supply quantities within the energy bids required by the BS mechanism.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["bidding.supply"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g07-ev-08"]}],"pi":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g07-ev-08","location":{"location_id":"src-d485825b0d-p27-c2r2__v141-a-M03-pricing","page":27,"printed_page":"1019","section":"A.2.3","anchor_text":"(A27) r agent under mid-market rate mechanism. energy cost and income evenly throughout the time hor","equation_id":"A28","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-27.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"Bill sharing is a mechanism in which all the prosumers share the energy cost and income evenly throughout the time horizon. The energy bids required by the BS mechanism are the same as those in the SDR mechanism as described by Formula (A18). The internal price is calculated by\n\n\\begin{cases} p_t^{buy} = r_t^{retail} \\cdot \\frac{\\sum_{t \\in T_u^+} \\sum_{n \\in \\mathcal{P}\\mathcal{A}} e_{n,t}^{bid}}{\\sum_{n \\in \\mathcal{P}\\mathcal{A}} \\sum_{t \\in T_l^+} e_{n,t}^{bid}}, & T_u^+ = \\{ t \\mid \\sum_{n \\in \\mathcal{P}\\mathcal{A}} e_{n,t}^{bid} > 0, t \\in T \\}, T_l^+ = \\{ t \\mid e_{n,t}^{bid} > 0, t \\in T \\} \\\\ p_t^{sell} = r_t^{export} \\cdot \\frac{\\sum_{t \\in T_u^-} \\sum_{n \\in \\mathcal{P}\\mathcal{A}} |e_{n,t}^{bid}|}{\\sum_{n \\in \\mathcal{P}\\mathcal{A}} \\sum_{t \\in T_l^-} |e_{n,t}^{bid}|}, & T_u^- = \\{ t \\mid \\sum_{n \\in \\mathcal{P}\\mathcal{A}} e_{n,t}^{bid} \u003c 0, t \\in T \\}, T_l^- = \\{ t \\mid e_{n,t}^{bid} \u003c 0, t \\in T \\} \\end{cases}  (A28)\n\nFormula (A28) actually distributes the total energy cost and income of the whole energy sharing region among the prosumers according the amount of energy they consume and generate. Taking the buying price part as an example, r_t^{retail} \\cdot \\sum_{t \\in T_u^+} \\sum_{n \\in \\mathcal{P}\\mathcal{A}} e_{n,t}^{bid} is the total energy cost of the whole region for importing electricity from the retailer throughout the time horizon, which is divided by \\sum_{n \\in \\mathcal{P}\\mathcal{A}} \\sum_{t \\in T_l^+} e_{n,t}^{bid}, the sum of each individual prosumer's total positive net energy consumption throughout the time horizon."}],"field_notes":{"empty_E_reason":"C explicitly supplied only source-backed unary facts for this function; other graph gaps remain reviewable.","empty_x_reason":"This rule specifies a submission-format requirement, not an optimization or operational decision. The source's decision variables x (controllable device statuses) belong to the prosumer decision-making model in Appendix A.1, not to this supply-submission constraint. No design-selection or operational variable is declared for this rule in the frozen graph.","empty_theta_reason":"No fixed input, coefficient, bound, or constant is declared for this rule in the frozen graph. Formula (A18) is referenced but not quoted with its parameters in the supplied evidence for this rule, so no source-supported parameter object is created."},"evidence_basis":"explicit","implementation_status":"unimplemented","status":"needs_review","lead_ids":["v141-a-M03-pricing","v141-a-M03-settlement"],"extras":{"decision_anchor":"bidding.supply","graph_fact_supports":[[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g07-ev-08","quote":"The energy bids required by the BS mechanism are the same as those in the SDR mechanism as described by Formula (A18)."}]],"C2_formalization":{"graph_sha256":"416825d30f3f24fc688dcd7c61aed28d134bdb6ac8014f724bf86d5f8d2f87da","applicability":"non_mathematical","reason":"The frozen rule expresses a procedural format requirement: energy bids required by the BS mechanism must use the same energy-bid format as SDR, described by Formula (A18). The supplied B evidence states this requirement explicitly but does not quote the full Formula (A18) definition or its symbol definitions. The frozen graph contains only the node bidding.supply and no edges or variable/parameter objects for this rule. Because the rule is a submission-format requirement rather than a mathematical optimization or pricing relation, it is treated as non-mathematical; the existing C1 procedural constraint is retained unchanged and not replaced by invented mathematics. B evidence remains unreviewed.","bindings":[{"object_id":"v141-c-R018-C001","node_ids":["bidding.supply"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"The procedural constraint governs the supply submission activity represented by the existing node bidding.supply. No edge is present in the frozen graph for this rule, and no mathematical relation is asserted."}],"revision_requests":["If a mathematical formalization of the BS supply bid is required, C.1 should add a verified evidence object for Formula (A18), because v141-b-g07-ev-08 references Formula (A18) but does not quote its full expression or symbol definitions.","To bind any future algebraic expression for the BS energy bid to the frozen graph, C.1 should register Formula (A18)'s symbols and the corresponding evidence locations, including e_{n,t}^{bid}, T, A_f, x^*_{δ,t}, x^{ch*}_t, x^{dis*}_t, P^{must-run}_t, P_{PV,t}, η^ch, and η^dis, with explicit same-mechanism evidence IDs.","C.1 should clarify whether v141-c-R018 is intended to remain a purely procedural format rule or to include the algebraic definition of the energy bid under BS; the present frozen graph supports only the procedural reading."]}},"quarantined_references":[]}});
